{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg936\deff0\uc1{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset134 \'cb\'ce\'cc\'e5;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset134 \'ba\'da\'cc\'e5;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;}\viewkind4\widowctrl\hyphauto0\pard\lang2052\f1\fs23 \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs34\sa70\qc \b \'c9\'cf\'ba\'a3\'ca\'d0\'d0\'a1\'d1\'a7\'c8\'fd\'c4\'ea\'bc\'b6\'d3\'a2\'d3\'ef\'d7\'db\'ba\'cf\'b8\'b4\'cf\'b0\'be\'ed\'a3\'a8\'b6\'fe\'a3\'a9\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs22\sa75\qc \'bb\'a6\'bd\'cc\'b0\'e6\'a1\'a4\'c8\'fd\'c4\'ea\'bc\'b6\'c9\'cf\'cf\'c2\'b2\'e1\'d7\'db\'ba\'cf\'d5\'ef\'b6\'cf\'a1\'a4\'cc\'e1\'b8\'df\'c1\'b7\'cf\'b0\'a3\'a82026\'c4\'ea8\'d4\'c2\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa100\ql \'d1\'a7\'d0\'a3\'a3\'ba____________\'a1\'a1\'b0\'e0\'bc\'b6\'a3\'ba____________\'a1\'a1\'d0\'d5\'c3\'fb\'a3\'ba____________\'a1\'a1\'d1\'a7\'ba\'c5\'a3\'ba____________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b I. Letters and sounds \'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'d3\'eb\'d3\'ef\'d2\'f4\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql A. Write the lowercase letters. \'d0\'b4\'b3\'f6\'b6\'d4\'d3\'a6\'b5\'c4\'d0\'a1\'d0\'b4\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. B ____\'a1\'a12. D ____\'a1\'a13. G ____\'a1\'a14. J ____\'a1\'a15. Q ____\'a1\'a16. R ____\'a1\'a17. Y ____\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql B. Write the capital letters. \'d0\'b4\'b3\'f6\'b6\'d4\'d3\'a6\'b5\'c4\'b4\'f3\'d0\'b4\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. h ____\'a1\'a12. k ____\'a1\'a13. m ____\'a1\'a14. p ____\'a1\'a15. t ____\'a1\'a16. w ____\'a1\'a17. z ____\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql C. Choose the word with a different vowel sound. \'d1\'a1\'b3\'f6\'d4\'aa\'d2\'f4\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'b7\'a2\'d2\'f4\'b2\'bb\'cd\'ac\'b5\'c4\'d2\'bb\'cf\'ee\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. (\'a1\'a1) A. cat\'a1\'a1B. bag\'a1\'a1C. cake\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. (\'a1\'a1) A. he\'a1\'a1B. pen\'a1\'a1C. red\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. (\'a1\'a1) A. bike\'a1\'a1B. fish\'a1\'a1C. kite\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. (\'a1\'a1) A. dog\'a1\'a1B. nose\'a1\'a1C. box\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. (\'a1\'a1) A. pupil\'a1\'a1B. sun\'a1\'a1C. duck\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b II. Vocabulary \'b4\'ca\'bb\'e3\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql A. Choose the odd one out. \'d1\'a1\'b3\'f6\'b2\'bb\'cd\'ac\'c0\'e0\'b5\'c4\'d2\'bb\'cf\'ee\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. (\'a1\'a1) A. juice\'a1\'a1B. water\'a1\'a1C. bread\'a1\'a1D. milk\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. (\'a1\'a1) A. shirt\'a1\'a1B. coat\'a1\'a1C. trousers\'a1\'a1D. tiger\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. (\'a1\'a1) A. spring\'a1\'a1B. summer\'a1\'a1C. warm\'a1\'a1D. winter\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. (\'a1\'a1) A. run\'a1\'a1B. jump\'a1\'a1C. sing\'a1\'a1D. book\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. (\'a1\'a1) A. uncle\'a1\'a1B. aunt\'a1\'a1C. cousin\'a1\'a1D. teacher\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. (\'a1\'a1) A. library\'a1\'a1B. classroom\'a1\'a1C. playground\'a1\'a1D. banana\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 7. (\'a1\'a1) A. eye\'a1\'a1B. ear\'a1\'a1C. nose\'a1\'a1D. tall\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 8. (\'a1\'a1) A. eleven\'a1\'a1B. twelve\'a1\'a1C. twenty\'a1\'a1D. pencil\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql B. Write the English words. \'b8\'f9\'be\'dd\'d6\'d0\'ce\'c4\'d0\'b4\'b5\'a5\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. \'bc\'d0\'bf\'cb\'c9\'c0 ________\'a1\'a12. \'c1\'ac\'d2\'c2\'c8\'b9 ________\'a1\'a13. \'b6\'cc\'bf\'e3 ________\'a1\'a14. \'ce\'a7\'bd\'ed ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. \'ca\'d6\'cc\'d7 ________\'a1\'a16. \'d2\'f5\'d3\'ea\'b5\'c4 ________\'a1\'a17. \'d0\'c7\'c6\'da\'cb\'c4 ________\'a1\'a18. \'ce\'e7\'b2\'cd ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 9. \'d0\'dc ________\'a1\'a110. \'b7\'c9\'bb\'fa ________\'a1\'a111. \'cd\'b7\'b7\'a2 ________\'a1\'a112. \'c7\'ef\'cc\'ec ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql C. Complete the words. \'b8\'f9\'be\'dd\'cc\'e1\'ca\'be\'b2\'b9\'c8\'ab\'b5\'a5\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. sw__ter \'c3\'ab\'d2\'c2\'a1\'a12. br__kfast \'d4\'e7\'b2\'cd\'a1\'a13. pl__ground \'b2\'d9\'b3\'a1\'a1\'a14. th__sty \'bf\'da\'bf\'ca\'b5\'c4\'a1\'a15. el__hant \'b4\'f3\'cf\'f3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. grandm__her \'c4\'cc\'c4\'cc/\'cd\'e2\'c6\'c5\'a1\'a17. w__ther \'cc\'ec\'c6\'f8\'a1\'a18. fav__rite \'d7\'ee\'cf\'b2\'bb\'b6\'b5\'c4\'a1\'a19. v__etable \'ca\'df\'b2\'cb\'a1\'a110. b__utiful \'c3\'c0\'c0\'f6\'b5\'c4\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql D. Choose and write. \'d1\'a1\'b4\'ca\'cc\'ee\'bf\'d5\'a3\'ac\'c3\'bf\'b4\'ca\'cf\'de\'d3\'c3\'d2\'bb\'b4\'ce\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql behind\'a1\'a1cloudy\'a1\'a1afraid\'a1\'a1breakfast\'a1\'a1Saturday\'a1\'a1teeth\'a1\'a1write\'a1\'a1winter\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. The mouse is ________ the box.\'a1\'a12. It is ________ today. Take an umbrella.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. I have ________ at seven.\'a1\'a14. The little rabbit is ________ of the wolf.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. We do not go to school on ________.\'a1\'a16. Brush your ________ every morning.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 7. I can ________ my name in English.\'a1\'a18. It is cold in ________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b III. Grammar and sentences \'d3\'ef\'b7\'a8\'d3\'eb\'be\'e4\'d0\'cd\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Choose the best answer. \'d1\'a1\'d4\'f1\'d7\'ee\'c7\'a1\'b5\'b1\'b5\'c4\'b4\'f0\'b0\'b8\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. (\'a1\'a1) This is ________ orange. A. a\'a1\'a1B. an\'a1\'a1C. the\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. (\'a1\'a1) My brother ________ a new football. A. have\'a1\'a1B. has\'a1\'a1C. is\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. (\'a1\'a1) The girls ________ in the classroom. A. am\'a1\'a1B. is\'a1\'a1C. are\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. (\'a1\'a1) Look at the ________. They are white. A. sheep\'a1\'a1B. sheeps\'a1\'a1C. a sheep\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. (\'a1\'a1) ________ is my English teacher, Miss Wang. A. He\'a1\'a1B. She\'a1\'a1C. It\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. (\'a1\'a1) \'a1\'aa Is this your ruler? \'a1\'aa No, it is not ________ ruler. A. my\'a1\'a1B. me\'a1\'a1C. I\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 7. (\'a1\'a1) I can see two birds ________ the tree. A. in\'a1\'a1B. at\'a1\'a1C. of\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 8. (\'a1\'a1) \'a1\'aa ________ pencils are there? \'a1\'aa Twelve. A. How old\'a1\'a1B. How much\'a1\'a1C. How many\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 9. (\'a1\'a1) \'a1\'aa ________ is the T-shirt? \'a1\'aa Forty yuan. A. How many\'a1\'a1B. How much\'a1\'a1C. What colour\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 10. (\'a1\'a1) Peter ________ like coffee. A. do not\'a1\'a1B. does not\'a1\'a1C. is not\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 11. (\'a1\'a1) ________ your mother like reading? A. Do\'a1\'a1B. Does\'a1\'a1C. Is\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 12. (\'a1\'a1) The dog can run, but it ________ fly. A. can\'a1\'a1B. cannot\'a1\'a1C. does\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 13. (\'a1\'a1) We have lunch ________ twelve o'clock. A. in\'a1\'a1B. on\'a1\'a1C. at\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 14. (\'a1\'a1) It is rainy. ________ your umbrella. A. Take\'a1\'a1B. Takes\'a1\'a1C. Taking\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 15. (\'a1\'a1) These ________ my new gloves. A. am\'a1\'a1B. is\'a1\'a1C. are\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 16. (\'a1\'a1) Kitty and I ________ good friends. A. am\'a1\'a1B. are\'a1\'a1C. is\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 17. (\'a1\'a1) My father is tall. ________ hair is short. A. His\'a1\'a1B. Her\'a1\'a1C. Its\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 18. (\'a1\'a1) \'a1\'aa Where are the books? \'a1\'aa ________ on the desk. A. It is\'a1\'a1B. They are\'a1\'a1C. There are\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 19. (\'a1\'a1) Ben gets up ________ the morning. A. at\'a1\'a1B. in\'a1\'a1C. on\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 20. (\'a1\'a1) I like ________ pictures after school. A. draw\'a1\'a1B. draws\'a1\'a1C. drawing\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b IV. Quick responses \'c7\'e9\'be\'b0\'d3\'a6\'b4\'f0\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Match the questions with the answers. \'bd\'ab\'ce\'ca\'be\'e4\'d3\'eb\'b4\'f0\'be\'e4\'c5\'e4\'b6\'d4\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. (\'a1\'a1) Whose cap is this?\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1 A. It is windy.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. (\'a1\'a1) What is the weather like?\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1 B. It is Tom's.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. (\'a1\'a1) Would you like some soup?\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1 C. At half past seven.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. (\'a1\'a1) What does your uncle do?\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1 D. Yes, please.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. (\'a1\'a1) When do you go to school?\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1 E. He is a firefighter.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. (\'a1\'a1) Where is my schoolbag?\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1 F. I like skating.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 7. (\'a1\'a1) What do you like doing?\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1 G. There are four.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 8. (\'a1\'a1) How many seasons are there?\'a1\'a1 H. It is under the chair.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b V. Language use \'d3\'ef\'d1\'d4\'d4\'cb\'d3\'c3\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql A. Choose the right word. \'d1\'a1\'d4\'f1\'d5\'fd\'c8\'b7\'b5\'c4\'b4\'ca\'cc\'ee\'bf\'d5\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. This is Alice. (She / Her) is my classmate.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. That is (we / our) classroom.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. The cat is white. (It / Its) eyes are blue.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. I have a brother. (His / Her) name is Sam.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. Are these (you / your) shoes?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. (They / Their) are my grandparents.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql B. Rewrite the sentences. \'c1\'ac\'b4\'ca\'b3\'c9\'be\'e4\'a3\'ac\'d7\'a2\'d2\'e2\'b4\'f3\'d0\'a1\'d0\'b4\'ba\'cd\'b1\'ea\'b5\'e3\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. weather / the / How / is / today (?)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. does / What / father / your / do (?)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. library / is / the / Where (?)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. elephants / like / I / big (.)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. breakfast / at / have / seven / We (.)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. kite / cannot / This / fly (.)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 7. are / Whose / these / socks (?)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 8. spring / warm / sunny / is / and (.)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 9. brother / football / My / playing / likes (.)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 10. any / there / Are / books / bag / the / in (?)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b VI. Complete the dialogues \'b2\'b9\'c8\'ab\'b6\'d4\'bb\'b0\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql A. At a clothes shop. \'b4\'d3\'b7\'bd\'bf\'f2\'d6\'d0\'d1\'a1\'be\'e4\'d7\'d3\'a3\'ac\'b0\'d1\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'d0\'b4\'d4\'da\'ba\'e1\'cf\'df\'c9\'cf\'a1\'a3\'d3\'d0\'d2\'bb\'cf\'ee\'b6\'e0\'d3\'e0\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql A. It is too big.\'a1\'a1B. May I try it on?\'a1\'a1C. Which one do you like?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql D. How much is it?\'a1\'a1E. I need a sweater.\'a1\'a1F. Here you are.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Shop assistant: Can I help you?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Jill: 1. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Shop assistant: The red one or the blue one?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Jill: 2. ________ I like blue.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Shop assistant: 3. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Jill: Thank you. 4. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Shop assistant: Of course.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Jill: It is nice. 5. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Shop assistant: Fifty yuan.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql B. Making a plan. \'b4\'d3\'b7\'bd\'bf\'f2\'d6\'d0\'d1\'a1\'be\'e4\'d7\'d3\'a3\'ac\'b0\'d1\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'d0\'b4\'d4\'da\'ba\'e1\'cf\'df\'c9\'cf\'a1\'a3\'d3\'d0\'d2\'bb\'cf\'ee\'b6\'e0\'d3\'e0\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql A. What can we do there?\'a1\'a1B. Shall we go to the park?\'a1\'a1C. See you tomorrow.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql D. What time shall we meet?\'a1\'a1E. I am sorry.\'a1\'a1F. It will be sunny.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Tom: What is the weather like tomorrow?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql May: 6. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Tom: Great! 7. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql May: Good idea.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Tom: 8. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql May: We can ride bikes and take photos.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Tom: 9. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql May: At nine o'clock at the school gate.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Tom: OK. 10. ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b VII. Reading \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'c0\'ed\'bd\'e2\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql A. Read and judge. \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'b6\'cc\'ce\'c4\'a3\'ac\'c5\'d0\'b6\'cf\'d5\'fd\'ce\'f3\'a3\'ac\'d3\'c3T\'bb\'f2F\'b1\'ed\'ca\'be\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Danny lives near his school. He gets up at a quarter past six. After breakfast, he walks to school with his sister. Classes begin at eight. He has Chinese, Maths, English and Art today. At noon, he eats rice, fish and vegetables at school. He plays table tennis after class. He goes home at half past four.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. (\'a1\'a1) Danny lives far from his school.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. (\'a1\'a1) Danny gets up at 6:15.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. (\'a1\'a1) He goes to school on foot.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. (\'a1\'a1) He has Music today.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. (\'a1\'a1) He has lunch at school.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. (\'a1\'a1) He goes home at 4:30.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql B. Read and choose. \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'b6\'cc\'ce\'c4\'a3\'ac\'d1\'a1\'d4\'f1\'d5\'fd\'c8\'b7\'b4\'f0\'b0\'b8\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql It is Saturday morning. The weather is cold and windy. Mum, Dad and Rose are going to Grandma's home. Mum wears a purple coat and a scarf. Dad wears a black jacket. Rose wears a warm sweater, a hat and gloves. They take some fruit and a cake for Grandma. They go there by bus.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. (\'a1\'a1) What day is it? A. Friday\'a1\'a1B. Saturday\'a1\'a1C. Sunday\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. (\'a1\'a1) How is the weather? A. Cold and windy\'a1\'a1B. Warm and sunny\'a1\'a1C. Cool and cloudy\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. (\'a1\'a1) What colour is Mum's coat? A. Black\'a1\'a1B. Red\'a1\'a1C. Purple\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. (\'a1\'a1) Who wears gloves? A. Mum\'a1\'a1B. Dad\'a1\'a1C. Rose\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. (\'a1\'a1) What do they take? A. Flowers and milk\'a1\'a1B. Fruit and a cake\'a1\'a1C. Bread and juice\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. (\'a1\'a1) How do they go? A. By bus\'a1\'a1B. By car\'a1\'a1C. On foot\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql C. Read the animal card and answer. \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'b6\'af\'ce\'ef\'d7\'ca\'c1\'cf\'bf\'a8\'a3\'ac\'d3\'c3\'d3\'a2\'ce\'c4\'bb\'d8\'b4\'f0\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Animal: African elephant\'a1\'a1Home: Africa\'a1\'a1Colour: grey\'a1\'a1Food: grass and leaves\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Body: very big, two large ears, a long nose\'a1\'a1Can: walk, run and swim\'a1\'a1Cannot: jump\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. Where does the African elephant live?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. What colour is it?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. What does it eat?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. Does it have small ears?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. What can it do?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. Can it jump?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql D. Read the timetable and answer. \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'bf\'ce\'b3\'cc\'b1\'ed\'a3\'ac\'bb\'d8\'b4\'f0\'ce\'ca\'cc\'e2\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Monday: Chinese, Maths, Art, PE\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Tuesday: English, Chinese, Music, Science\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Wednesday: Maths, English, PE, Art\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Thursday: Chinese, Maths, Science, Music\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Friday: English, Chinese, Maths, Class Meeting\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. How many lessons are there every day?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. What lessons does Jack have on Tuesday?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 3. When does Jack have Art?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 4. Does Jack have PE on Thursday?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 5. How many English lessons does he have in a week?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 6. Which subject does he have every school day?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 7. Jack likes experiments. Which two days may be his favourite? Why?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql E. Read and complete. \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'b6\'cc\'ce\'c4\'a3\'ac\'b4\'d3\'b7\'bd\'bf\'f2\'d6\'d0\'d1\'a1\'b4\'ca\'cc\'ee\'bf\'d5\'a3\'ac\'c3\'bf\'b4\'ca\'cf\'de\'d3\'c3\'d2\'bb\'b4\'ce\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql plants\'a1\'a1water\'a1\'a1small\'a1\'a1sunny\'a1\'a1garden\'a1\'a1helps\'a1\'a1tomatoes\'a1\'a1happy\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql Lucy has a 1. ________ behind her house. It is not big, but it is beautiful. She 2. ________ flowers and vegetables there. Every 3. ________ morning, she gives them some 4. ________. Her grandfather 5. ________ her. In summer, they can pick red 6. ________. Lucy puts some on a 7. ________ plate and gives them to her neighbours. Everyone is 8. ________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs26\sa70\sb135\ql \b VIII. Writing \'d0\'b4\'d7\'f7\'a3\'a8\'c8\'ce\'d1\'a1\'d2\'bb\'cc\'e2\'a3\'a9\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 1. My school day\'a3\'ba\'d3\'c35\'a1\'aa7\'be\'e4\'bb\'b0\'bd\'e9\'c9\'dc\'c4\'e3\'b5\'c4\'c9\'cf\'d1\'a7\'c8\'d5\'a3\'ac\'bf\'c9\'d0\'b4\'c6\'f0\'b4\'b2\'ca\'b1\'bc\'e4\'a1\'a2\'c9\'cf\'d1\'a7\'b7\'bd\'ca\'bd\'a1\'a2\'bf\'ce\'b3\'cc\'a1\'a2\'ce\'e7\'b2\'cd\'ba\'cd\'b7\'c5\'d1\'a7\'ba\'f3\'b5\'c4\'bb\'ee\'b6\'af\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql 2. My favourite animal\'a3\'ba\'d3\'c35\'a1\'aa7\'be\'e4\'bb\'b0\'bd\'e9\'c9\'dc\'d2\'bb\'d6\'d6\'cf\'b2\'bb\'b6\'b5\'c4\'b6\'af\'ce\'ef\'a3\'ac\'bf\'c9\'d0\'b4\'cd\'e2\'d0\'ce\'a1\'a2\'d1\'d5\'c9\'ab\'a1\'a2\'ca\'b3\'ce\'ef\'a1\'a2\'c4\'dc\'c1\'a6\'ba\'cd\'cf\'b2\'bb\'b6\'cb\'fc\'b5\'c4\'d4\'ad\'d2\'f2\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa52\ql \'d2\'aa\'c7\'f3\'a3\'ba\'be\'e4\'d7\'d3\'cd\'ea\'d5\'fb\'a3\'ac\'b4\'f3\'d0\'a1\'d0\'b4\'ba\'cd\'b1\'ea\'b5\'e3\'d5\'fd\'c8\'b7\'a3\'ac\'be\'a1\'c1\'bf\'b2\'bb\'d2\'aa\'c1\'ac\'d0\'f8\'ca\'b9\'d3\'c3\'cd\'ea\'c8\'ab\'cf\'e0\'cd\'ac\'b5\'c4\'be\'e4\'d0\'cd\'a1\'a3\par \page \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs30\sa100\qc \b \'b2\'ce\'bf\'bc\'b4\'f0\'b0\'b8\'a3\'a8\'b9\'a9\'bc\'d2\'b3\'a4\'ba\'cb\'b6\'d4\'a3\'a9\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa I. Letters and sounds\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql A. 1. b\'a1\'a12. d\'a1\'a13. g\'a1\'a14. j\'a1\'a15. q\'a1\'a16. r\'a1\'a17. y\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql B. 1. H\'a1\'a12. K\'a1\'a13. M\'a1\'a14. P\'a1\'a15. T\'a1\'a16. W\'a1\'a17. Z\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql C. 1. C\'a1\'a12. A\'a1\'a13. B\'a1\'a14. B\'a1\'a15. A\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa II. Vocabulary\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql A. 1. C\'a1\'a12. D\'a1\'a13. C\'a1\'a14. D\'a1\'a15. D\'a1\'a16. D\'a1\'a17. D\'a1\'a18. D\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql B. 1. jacket\'a1\'a12. dress\'a1\'a13. shorts\'a1\'a14. scarf\'a1\'a15. gloves\'a1\'a16. rainy\'a1\'a17. Thursday\'a1\'a18. lunch\'a1\'a19. bear\'a1\'a110. plane\'a1\'a111. hair\'a1\'a112. autumn\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql C. 1. ea\'a1\'a12. ea\'a1\'a13. ay\'a1\'a14. ir\'a1\'a15. ep\'a1\'a16. ot\'a1\'a17. ea\'a1\'a18. ou\'a1\'a19. eg\'a1\'a110. ea\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql D. 1. behind\'a1\'a12. cloudy\'a1\'a13. breakfast\'a1\'a14. afraid\'a1\'a15. Saturday\'a1\'a16. teeth\'a1\'a17. write\'a1\'a18. winter\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa III. Grammar and sentences\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. B\'a1\'a12. B\'a1\'a13. C\'a1\'a14. A\'a1\'a15. B\'a1\'a16. A\'a1\'a17. A\'a1\'a18. C\'a1\'a19. B\'a1\'a110. B\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 11. B\'a1\'a112. B\'a1\'a113. C\'a1\'a114. A\'a1\'a115. C\'a1\'a116. B\'a1\'a117. A\'a1\'a118. B\'a1\'a119. B\'a1\'a120. C\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa IV. Quick responses\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. B\'a1\'a12. A\'a1\'a13. D\'a1\'a14. E\'a1\'a15. C\'a1\'a16. H\'a1\'a17. F\'a1\'a18. G\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa V. Language use\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql A. 1. She\'a1\'a12. our\'a1\'a13. Its\'a1\'a14. His\'a1\'a15. your\'a1\'a16. They\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql B. 1. How is the weather today?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 2. What does your father do?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 3. Where is the library?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 4. I like big elephants.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 5. We have breakfast at seven.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 6. This kite cannot fly.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 7. Whose socks are these?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 8. Spring is warm and sunny.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 9. My brother likes playing football.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 10. Are there any books in the bag?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa VI. Complete the dialogues\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. E\'a1\'a12. C\'a1\'a13. F\'a1\'a14. B\'a1\'a15. D\'a1\'a16. F\'a1\'a17. B\'a1\'a18. A\'a1\'a19. D\'a1\'a110. C\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa VII. Reading A\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. F\'a1\'a12. T\'a1\'a13. T\'a1\'a14. F\'a1\'a15. T\'a1\'a16. T\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa VII. Reading B\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. B\'a1\'a12. A\'a1\'a13. C\'a1\'a14. C\'a1\'a15. B\'a1\'a16. A\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa VII. Reading C\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. It lives in Africa.\'a1\'a12. It is grey.\'a1\'a13. It eats grass and leaves.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 4. No, it does not. It has two large ears.\'a1\'a15. It can walk, run and swim.\'a1\'a16. No, it cannot.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa VII. Reading D\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. There are four lessons every day.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 2. He has English, Chinese, Music and Science.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 3. He has Art on Monday and Wednesday.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 4. No, he does not.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 5. He has three English lessons in a week.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 6. He has Chinese every school day.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 7. Tuesday and Thursday, because he has Science on these two days.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa VII. Reading E\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql 1. garden\'a1\'a12. plants\'a1\'a13. sunny\'a1\'a14. water\'a1\'a15. helps\'a1\'a16. tomatoes\'a1\'a17. small\'a1\'a18. happy\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa55\sb90\ql \b Answer Key \'a1\'aa VIII. Writing\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql Sample 1: My school day\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql I get up at half past six. I walk to school with my friend. I have Chinese, Maths, English and PE. I have rice and vegetables for lunch. After school, I play basketball. I go home at half past four. I like my school day.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql Sample 2: My favourite animal\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql My favourite animal is the panda. It is black and white. It has a fat body. It likes bamboo. It can climb trees. It is quiet and lovely. I like it very much.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs21\sa42\ql \'c6\'c0\'d4\'c4\'ca\'b1\'d6\'d8\'b5\'e3\'bc\'ec\'b2\'e9\'a3\'ba\'c4\'da\'c8\'dd\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'b8\'b2\'b8\'c7\'cc\'e2\'c4\'bf\'d2\'aa\'b5\'e3\'a3\'ac\'d6\'f7\'ce\'bd\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'b4\'ee\'c5\'e4\'a3\'ac\'b5\'a5\'b8\'b4\'ca\'fd\'a1\'a2\'b4\'f3\'d0\'a1\'d0\'b4\'a1\'a2\'c6\'b4\'d0\'b4\'ba\'cd\'be\'e4\'c4\'a9\'b1\'ea\'b5\'e3\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'d5\'fd\'c8\'b7\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa55\sb130\ql \b \'b8\'f8\'bc\'d2\'b3\'a4\'b5\'c4\'d7\'a2\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs20\sa0\ql \'b1\'be\'be\'ed\'b8\'b2\'b8\'c7\'c8\'fd\'c4\'ea\'bc\'b6\'b3\'a3\'bc\'fb\'b5\'c4\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'ca\'e9\'d0\'b4\'a1\'a2\'bb\'f9\'b4\'a1\'d3\'ef\'d2\'f4\'a1\'a2\'d6\'f7\'cc\'e2\'b4\'ca\'bb\'e3\'a1\'a2\'c3\'fb\'b4\'ca\'b5\'a5\'b8\'b4\'ca\'fd\'a1\'a2\'b4\'fa\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a2have/has\'a1\'a2be\'b6\'af\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a2can\'a1\'a2\'d2\'bb\'b0\'e3\'d2\'c9\'ce\'ca\'be\'e4\'a1\'a2\'cc\'d8\'ca\'e2\'d2\'c9\'ce\'ca\'be\'e4\'a1\'a2\'bd\'e9\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a2\'c7\'e9\'be\'b0\'b6\'d4\'bb\'b0\'a1\'a2\'c1\'ac\'b4\'ca\'b3\'c9\'be\'e4\'a1\'a2\'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'ba\'cd\'d0\'b4\'d7\'f7\'a1\'a3\'d5\'eb\'b6\'d4\'c9\'cf\'d2\'bb\'b7\'dd\'b4\'ed\'cc\'e2\'a3\'ac\'b5\'da\'b6\'fe\'b4\'f3\'cc\'e2A\'d3\'c3\'c8\'ab\'d0\'c2\'b5\'c4\'b4\'ca\'d7\'e9\'bc\'cc\'d0\'f8\'bc\'ec\'b2\'e9\'b5\'a5\'b4\'ca\'b7\'d6\'c0\'e0\'c4\'dc\'c1\'a6\'a3\'ac\'b5\'da\'b6\'fe\'b4\'f3\'cc\'e2B\'a1\'a2C\'bc\'af\'d6\'d0\'c7\'bf\'bb\'af\'d2\'c2\'ce\'ef\'c0\'e0\'b4\'ca\'bb\'e3\'a3\'ac\'b2\'a2\'d3\'c3\'b2\'b9\'c8\'ab\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'b5\'c4\'b7\'bd\'ca\'bd\'d4\'d9\'b4\'ce\'bc\'ec\'b2\'e9sweater\'b5\'c4\'c6\'b4\'d0\'b4\'a1\'a3\'ce\'e5\'d7\'e9\'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'b7\'d6\'b1\'f0\'bc\'ec\'b2\'e9\'ca\'c2\'ca\'b5\'c5\'d0\'b6\'cf\'a1\'a2\'cc\'ec\'c6\'f8\'d3\'eb\'d2\'c2\'d7\'c5\'d0\'c5\'cf\'a2\'a1\'a2\'d7\'ca\'c1\'cf\'bf\'a8\'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'a1\'a2\'bf\'ce\'b3\'cc\'b1\'ed\'d0\'c5\'cf\'a2\'cc\'e1\'c8\'a1\'ba\'cd\'d3\'ef\'be\'b3\'d1\'a1\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a3\'bd\'a8\'d2\'e9\'b0\'d1\'b4\'ed\'ce\'f3\'b7\'d6\'ce\'aa\'a1\'b0\'b4\'ca\'d2\'e5\'b2\'bb\'c7\'e5\'a1\'a2\'c6\'b4\'d0\'b4\'b2\'bb\'c0\'ce\'a1\'a2\'be\'e4\'d0\'cd\'b2\'bb\'bb\'e1\'a1\'a2\'c2\'a9\'b6\'c1\'d0\'c5\'cf\'a2\'a1\'a2\'b4\'f0\'be\'e4\'b2\'bb\'cd\'ea\'d5\'fb\'a1\'b1\'ce\'e5\'c0\'e0\'bc\'c7\'c2\'bc\'a1\'a3\'cc\'fd\'c1\'a6\'b2\'bf\'b7\'d6\'c8\'d4\'c2\'d4\'a1\'a3\par }